ROCKET_DASHBOARD_URL=http://localhost:3000
SQLITE_PATH=work/rocket1000.sqlite
# Production operator settings; never entered by the EA user:
# ROCKET_DASHBOARD_URL=https://your-dashboard.example
# ROCKET_BACKEND_URL=https://your-dashboard.example
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://... (shared database required on Vercel)
# ROCKET_REQUIRE_POSTGRES=1
# Set OPENAI_API_KEY as a Production Secret in the existing Vercel project.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=... (server-only; never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_)
# Paid-key Settings uses direct OpenAI only. The saved workspace key takes priority;
# removing it prevents an environment key or Gateway from silently reactivating it.
# ROCKET_OPENAI_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<canonical base64 of 32 cryptographically random bytes>
# Keep that encryption secret separate from the database and API key. Set the same
# secret on the web server and supervised analysis worker; never prefix NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-6.1-sol (configurable reasoning model; real account probe required)
# ROCKET_AI_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=2 (default app budget, USD per UTC day)
# Optional verified pricing for a model outside the built-in price catalog:
# ROCKET_AI_INPUT_USD_PER_MILLION=...
# ROCKET_AI_OUTPUT_USD_PER_MILLION=...
# Run npm run worker:analysis as a separate supervised service using the SAME
# PostgreSQL DATABASE_URL and encryption secret as the Vercel application.
# Optional protected scheduler endpoint /api/internal/ai-engine requires HTTPS:
# CRON_SECRET=<at least 32 random characters, managed only by the operator>
# It is not scheduled just by setting a secret; the app requires actual check-ins.
# On Vercel, ROCKET_QUEUE_ANALYSIS=1 enables the registered durable Queue consumer.
# Queue callbacks must genuinely check in before Start; no extra worker secret is used.
# No email/password authentication, signup switch, or master signing key is used.
